{
  "durationSeconds": 128,
  "bytes": 8257531,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 11.441,
      "title": "Where does 42.0 travel?"
    },
    {
      "id": "s02",
      "start": 11.441,
      "end": 26.509,
      "title": "Storage is separate from execution"
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "start": 26.509,
      "end": 39.295,
      "title": "The launch requests one thread"
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "start": 39.295,
      "end": 54.0,
      "title": "An SM executes the kernel"
    },
    {
      "id": "s05",
      "start": 54.0,
      "end": 69.437,
      "title": "The assignment writes device storage"
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "start": 69.437,
      "end": 81.32,
      "title": "Copy the result into CPU memory"
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "start": 81.32,
      "end": 95.051,
      "title": "The CPU prints its own copy"
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "start": 95.051,
      "end": 109.951,
      "title": "Predict a changed value"
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "start": 109.951,
      "end": 127.635,
      "title": "New data, the same launch"
    }
  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "id": "s01-c1",
      "start": 0.6,
      "end": 2.947,
      "text": "The Console shows forty-two point zero."
    },
    {
      "id": "s01-c2",
      "start": 3.167,
      "end": 5.407,
      "text": "But the GPU does not print that line."
    },
    {
      "id": "s01-c3",
      "start": 5.627,
      "end": 10.021,
      "text": "Follow the value from the kernel to device memory, then back to the CPU."
    },
    {
      "id": "s02-c1",
      "start": 12.041,
      "end": 17.033,
      "text": "On this simplified discrete GPU, the compute chip and device memory are separate."
    },
    {
      "id": "s02-c2",
      "start": 17.253,
      "end": 19.728,
      "text": "The CPU reserves space for one float."
    },
    {
      "id": "s02-c3",
      "start": 19.948,
      "end": 25.089,
      "text": "The pointer output identifies that space; allocating it does not execute hello."
    },
    {
      "id": "s03-c1",
      "start": 27.109,
      "end": 30.992,
      "text": "The CPU submits a launch: one block containing one thread."
    },
    {
      "id": "s03-c2",
      "start": 31.212,
      "end": 33.473,
      "text": "These numbers describe logical work."
    },
    {
      "id": "s03-c3",
      "start": 33.693,
      "end": 37.875,
      "text": "They do not select a physical processor or reserve the whole GPU."
    },
    {
      "id": "s04-c1",
      "start": 39.895,
      "end": 44.865,
      "text": "The block is assigned to a streaming multiprocessor, or SM, on the compute chip."
    },
    {
      "id": "s04-c2",
      "start": 45.085,
      "end": 48.285,
      "text": "Its execution hardware runs the thread's instructions."
    },
    {
      "id": "s04-c3",
      "start": 48.505,
      "end": 52.58,
      "text": "A thread is an execution of code, not a dedicated piece of hardware."
    },
    {
      "id": "s05-c1",
      "start": 54.6,
      "end": 59.357,
      "text": "The assignment stores forty-two point zero at the address for output index zero."
    },
    {
      "id": "s05-c2",
      "start": 59.577,
      "end": 62.265,
      "text": "The value belongs to the GPU allocation."
    },
    {
      "id": "s05-c3",
      "start": 62.485,
      "end": 65.152,
      "text": "It is not yet the CPU variable value."
    },
    {
      "id": "s05-c4",
      "start": 65.372,
      "end": 68.017,
      "text": "Cache details are omitted from this data path."
    },
    {
      "id": "s06-c1",
      "start": 70.037,
      "end": 75.755,
      "text": "This device-to-host copy waits for the result and places it in the CPU variable value."
    },
    {
      "id": "s06-c2",
      "start": 75.975,
      "end": 79.9,
      "text": "The launch statement by itself did not mean the kernel had already finished."
    },
    {
      "id": "s07-c1",
      "start": 81.92,
      "end": 84.032,
      "text": "Now main prints its CPU copy."
    },
    {
      "id": "s07-c2",
      "start": 84.252,
      "end": 88.433,
      "text": "The SM executed the assignment, device storage held the result,"
    },
    {
      "id": "s07-c3",
      "start": 88.653,
      "end": 91.725,
      "text": "and the copy made that result available to the CPU."
    },
    {
      "id": "s07-c4",
      "start": 91.945,
      "end": 93.631,
      "text": "These are three different roles."
    },
    {
      "id": "s08-c1",
      "start": 95.651,
      "end": 99.576,
      "text": "Pause and predict: if the assignment stores thirteen point zero,"
    },
    {
      "id": "s08-c2",
      "start": 99.796,
      "end": 101.609,
      "text": "does the launch need more threads?"
    },
    {
      "id": "s08-c3",
      "start": 101.829,
      "end": 104.731,
      "text": "Which value will the CPU print after the copy?"
    },
    {
      "id": "s09-c1",
      "start": 110.551,
      "end": 112.428,
      "text": "The launch still requests one thread."
    },
    {
      "id": "s09-c2",
      "start": 112.648,
      "end": 114.589,
      "text": "Only the stored value changes."
    },
    {
      "id": "s09-c3",
      "start": 114.809,
      "end": 119.887,
      "text": "In hello in the CUDA source editor, set the stored value to thirteen point zero f."
    },
    {
      "id": "s09-c4",
      "start": 120.107,
      "end": 122.752,
      "text": "Click Compile and run, and inspect Console."
    },
    {
      "id": "s09-c5",
      "start": 122.972,
      "end": 126.215,
      "text": "Leave the allocation, copy and error checks unchanged."
    }
  ],
